            {
              "kind": "mapping",
              "tag": "!!map",
              "head": "# Opt-in PVE multi-storage placement, selected via the `pve-storage-sets`\n# feature. Loaded AFTER overlay/cpis/pve-base.yml (blueprint.pm processes the\n# IaaS baseline files before the feature loop), so the director's own pve\n# property block already exists and these replace? paths land inside it.\n#\n# Every op targets /instance_groups/name=bosh/properties/pve only. There is\n# deliberately no cloud_provider counterpart, unlike pve-ha-proto.yml. The CPI\n# refuses a set-managed placement until it can lock\n# storage_allocation_journal_dir, and during `bosh create-env` the CPI runs on\n# the operator's workstation or the bastion, where /var/vcap/store does not\n# exist and nothing provisions it. The director VM keeps scalar placement for\n# its own root and persistent disks, and storage sets take over for every VM\n# the director goes on to create.\n#\n# The three optional CPI keys this feature does not model -- root_storage_set,\n# require_disjoint_storage_sets, and storage_status_max_age_seconds -- are set\n# through bosh-configs.director-cpi when an env ever needs them. See MANUAL.md.\n\n# The director runs its CPI calls inside BPM worker processes, and BPM gives\n# each job only its own store directory, so the journal directory is invisible\n# to the CPI until the director job mounts it. director.cpi_additional_volumes\n# is appended to every worker's unrestricted_volumes by the bosh release's\n# jobs/director/templates/bpm.yml, alongside the CPI job and log directories it\n# derives from director.cpi_job. writable: true because the CPI locks and\n# writes the journal, and mount_only: true because the pve_cpi job's own\n# pre-start already creates the directory as vcap with mode 0700 and BPM must\n# not create it first with different ownership.\n#\n# This is the only place the kit sets cpi_additional_volumes, so the list is\n# written whole rather than appended to. It reuses the same journal-dir\n# variable the properties below use, so the mount and the property cannot drift\n# apart.",
